                "height": 252.0,
                "is_export": false,
                "layername": "0. Introduction",
                "max_width": 600,
                "min_height": 12,
                "min_width": 12,
                "no_export": false,
                "obj_args": null,
                "obj_name": "text_005",
                "obj_state": 3,
                "obj_type": "text",
                "panel_enable": false,
                "panel_x": 60.0,
                "panel_y": 151.0,
                "panel_z": 0,
                "patch_x": 60.0,
                "patch_y": 151.0,
                "patch_z": 0,
                "position_x": 60.0,
                "position_y": 151.0,
                "position_z": 0,
                "properties": {},
                "save_in_preset": false,
                "scope": "__patch__",
                "style": {},
                "update_required": true,
                "value": "This tutorial uses MFP \"layers\" as pages. A patch always has one or more layers; only one layer is visible at a time.\n\nYou should see a list of them in the <b>Layer</b> menu on the main menu bar. To advance through the tutorial, you can either click on the desired page in the Layer menu, or use the Page Down/Page Up keys to move to the next/previous page.\n\nNote that some instructions in the tutorial will \"jump\" away from the tutorial, requiring you to navigate back by clicking on the tutorial patch before proceeding. Do not be alarmed.\n\nIf the tutorial patch is not visible, you can select \"tutorial.help\" from the Window menu to return to it.\n\nInstructions labeled with the \"TIP\" callout are your tutorial steps. \n\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Press the Page Down (aka <b>PGDN</b>) key now to get started\n",
                "width": 599.0
            },
            "initargs": null,
            "midi_filters": null,
            "midi_mode": null,
            "name": "text_005",
            "osc_methods": [],
            "presets": {},
            "properties": {},
            "type": "text",
            "value": "This tutorial uses MFP \"layers\" as pages. A patch always has one or more layers; only one layer is visible at a time.\n\nYou should see a list of them in the <b>Layer</b> menu on the main menu bar. To advance through the tutorial, you can either click on the desired page in the Layer menu, or use the Page Down/Page Up keys to move to the next/previous page.\n\nNote that some instructions in the tutorial will \"jump\" away from the tutorial, requiring you to navigate back by clicking on the tutorial patch before proceeding. Do not be alarmed.\n\nIf the tutorial patch is not visible, you can select \"tutorial.help\" from the Window menu to return to it.\n\nInstructions labeled with the \"TIP\" callout are your tutorial steps. \n\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Press the Page Down (aka <b>PGDN</b>) key now to get started\n"
        },
