                "position_x": 62.0,
                "position_y": 82.0,
                "position_z": 0,
                "properties": {},
                "save_in_preset": false,
                "scope": "__patch__",
                "style": {},
                "update_required": true,
                "value": "The <b>[for]</b> object is key to iteration.  It splits a list of inputs into \nits elements and outputs them one at a time.  The items to iterate over \ncan be either init args (in the processor box) or received either inlet.\n\nIteration starts when a Bang, True, or an iterable is received on the left (hot) inlet.\n\nIteration will stop when the current list is traversed or a False is receved on\nthe left inlet. ",
                "width": 564.0
            },
            "initargs": null,
            "midi_filters": null,
            "midi_mode": null,
            "name": "text_039",
            "osc_methods": [],
            "presets": {},
            "properties": {},
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The <b>[for]</b> object is key to iteration.  It splits a list of inputs into \nits elements and outputs them one at a time.  The items to iterate over \ncan be either init args (in the processor box) or received either inlet.\n\nIteration starts when a Bang, True, or an iterable is received on the left (hot) inlet.\n\nIteration will stop when the current list is traversed or a False is receved on\nthe left inlet. "
        },
